  fishName: Cloudclam
  description: The actual body of the cloudclam is surprisingly small- the majority
    of its bulk is made up of a cotton-candy like fur that seems to have evolved
    to blend in with Nimbus 's clouds. Because of this, there is a persistant myth
    that Nimbus actually began as a cloudclam, which grew to a gigantic size only
    after millions of years.\n\n  Chef's Notes:\nThe fur makes for an excellent garnish,
    and the spindly little body inside can be turned to jerky.
